Thu Oct 08 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - krism <krism@opensuse.org>

- Review candidate, no RPM publication/version bump:
  - Allow confirmed SOURCE rollback for boot-mismatch/target-active-or-default.
  - Keep recovery context across interruption; identify rollback snapshots by TXID.
  - Account for shared free space by filesystem UUID and print abort reasons.
  - Normalize zero RPM epochs, require tukit --description and batch RPM queries.
  - Remove optional unfiltered payload verification; rename history helper.
  - Propagate XML canonicalization and Snapper inspection errors.
  - Fix unstaged rollback recovery across changed boot IDs without relaxing
    same-boot validation for staged rollback adoption.
  - Add 20 mocked regressions; real VM interruption/boot matrix remains pending.

- 5.7.1: sole supported offline atomic-update engine (development candidate).
- New independent state schema 1, with unversioned persistent state, cache,
  log and lock paths. No legacy state migration or multi-version support.
- Manual PREPARED -> REVALIDATED -> tukit TARGET -> verification -> reboot flow.
- Preserve manifest, protected core packages, bootability and explicit rollback.
- Add semantic capability checks and typed needs-inspection recovery.
- Fix find_owned_targets status propagation and fail-closed clear-opening when
  Snapper listing fails or any owned TARGET is present.
- Make df output validity explicit; remove unused preflight probes and helpers.
- Remove unused transaction state timestamps; history remains persistent.
- No timer, daemon or unattended scheduler.
- Candidate is not production-stable until VM failure/recovery matrix passes.
